        "trackId": "wy_nc_1401",
        "affectedElement": "packet_components",
        "question": "Which unpublished local filing preferences apply in the court where this petition will be filed: local cover sheet, copy count, electronic versus paper filing, filing method, chambers copy, whether the proposed Order for Expungement is submitted with the initial filing or later, any unpublished local template, any unpublished additional service document, and other court-specific filing mechanics. This is the narrowed remainder of the original packet-assembly question, which asked which Wyoming courts publish local expungement templates. The published half is answered: Wyoming publishes no statewide petition form and no statewide proposed-order template, and Casper Municipal Court is the only publicly identified local-form exception, whose packets bind that court alone. What remains is unpublished preference, which is filing mechanics rather than the legal document, so it is release-level and does not block generation of the statewide verified petition and proposed order. It is owned by rcap-wy-local-template-and-handout-survey, which remains open: no Wyoming county has been telephoned and the survey must not be recorded as complete. Escalation: if a county's answer changes the statewide legal document rather than only how it is filed, that exact issue returns to legal design before release."
      }
